{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"antsy-restored-seaslug","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Client report\n`AGENTS.md` and the setup/onboarding documentation do not tell a new contributor to run `rebar identity create --self` before using gates that sign attestations. A correctly installed checkout can therefore reach a signing gate without the local identity prerequisite and fail only at gate time.\n\nThe documentation gap is reported by a client project. Investigation must first confirm which supported bootstrap flows create an identity automatically, which gates require one, and whether `identity create --self` is universally correct or conditional on repository policy.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce onboarding from a clean temporary home/config using the documented setup path and the first signing gate.\n- Trace the identity lookup/error path and inventory every authoritative setup surface (`AGENTS.md`, local-dev/setup guides, contributor guide, packaged explanations).\n- Confirm the intended prerequisite and placement before editing docs.\n- Add a documentation/CLI contract test or rendered-help assertion at the smallest tier that fails when all setup paths omit the prerequisite.\n- Update each authoritative onboarding surface without duplicating contradictory guidance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A clean-environment reproduction identifies the first signing operation that fails and the exact missing identity state.\n- [ ] The intended use and scope of `rebar identity create --self` are cited from implementation/help or an approved identity contract.\n- [ ] Every authoritative setup/onboarding path either creates the identity or instructs the user when and how to run `rebar identity create --self`.\n- [ ] The guidance explains how to verify the identity and distinguishes repository-local versus user-global state as applicable.\n- [ ] A gating test detects regression of the prerequisite guidance without asserting incidental prose formatting.\n- [ ] Existing install/bootstrap flows that already provision identity remain accurate and are not duplicated or contradicted.","id":"cd53-c62e-7bac-4ed2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["client-report","documentation","identity","signing"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Setup docs omit rebar identity create --self before signing gates"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787067279813659001,"uuid":"b779411f-257c-46b8-b710-1369fcd85cd9"}